pagelike is an independent, open-source implementation of the protocol and
document model of PageLove (https://pagelove.com). It is not affiliated with,
sponsored by or endorsed by PageLove. "PageLove" is used only to describe
compatibility; it and any related marks belong to their owner.

pagelike was written from PageLove's public documentation, its public
MIT-licensed client libraries and example applications
(https://github.com/pagelove), and black-box observation of the hosted
service. It contains no PageLove server code.

Bundled third-party material:

- internal/selector: a modified copy of github.com/andybalholm/cascadia
  v1.3.5 (BSD-2-Clause); see internal/selector/NOTICE and
  internal/selector/LICENSE.cascadia.
- internal/liquid/testdata: unmodified files from PageLove's MIT-licensed
  example apps pagelove-polls and pagelove-shop (Copyright (c) 2026
  Pagelove), used as test fixtures; each directory carries its LICENSE.
  See internal/liquid/NOTICE.

